<p><strong>You can see staff performance without guessing when revenue, attendance and discounts are recorded per person and per branch as the work happens, then read in a single report.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The gut-feel review</h2>
<p>It is review time. You believe one therapist is your best, but another brings in more repeat customers, and a third has been absent more than you remembered. Without records, you decide by feeling, and the team can tell.</p>
<h2>Why it happens</h2>
<ul><li>Bookings are not tied to a named staff member.</li><li>Attendance and revenue are in different places.</li><li>Discounts are not linked to the person who gave them.</li></ul>
<h2>How it is solved</h2>
<p>Every booking in Zennly belongs to a named staff member and a branch, and every discount is recorded with who requested and approved it. <a href="/features/reports/">Reports</a> cover revenue, staff performance, discounts, attendance and referrals across every branch. See the <a href="/features/operational-visibility/">multi-branch dashboard</a> for a live view.</p>
<h2>Fairer reviews and pay</h2>
<p>Because <a href="/features/payroll/">commission</a> is calculated from completed, paid bookings, pay and reports tell the same story.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Tie every booking to the named staff member who did it.</li><li>Record attendance daily.</li><li>Look at revenue, absences and discounts together once a month.</li></ol>
